    but it gets cramped on narrow screens.
  - [1mC:[0m Same as A, plus a "Show failed sign-ins" button that sets the select to that type in one click. It's aimed at the
    support tickets, but it's one more control to build and review.

  I'd go with A. It matches the label-above-control rule in the guidelines and leaves room for a second filter later. C
  is worth it if the failed sign-in case matters enough to get its own button.

  Click one in the tab if you like, then reply here.

  The mockups are stored in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m, which is untracked and not in a [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet. You may want to add
  [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m to [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m so it doesn't end up in a commit. I haven't changed that file.

